# Windsurf Token Optimization Rules
# Optimized for Windsurf AI coding assistant

## Conversation Management
- Start new conversations for different tasks
- Clear context when switching between unrelated features
- Use /reset when conversation becomes too long

## Prompt Efficiency
- Use single-line requests when possible
- Avoid multi-step instructions in one prompt
- Be specific: "fix bug in line 42" not "there's a bug somewhere"

## File Operations
- Use @file to reference files instead of pasting content
- Request specific file operations: "update function X in file Y"
- Avoid asking to "read and understand" - just state what needs changing

## Code Generation
- Request minimal viable implementations
- Ask for specific patterns: "use try-except here"
- Avoid "make it production-ready" - be specific about requirements

## Debugging
- Provide error messages and stack traces directly
- Specify exact line numbers when possible
- Ask for specific fixes: "handle this exception" not "fix error handling"

## Token-Saving Commands
- Use /compact to compress conversation history
- Use /focus to limit context to current task
- Use /clear to remove unnecessary context
